[1mDifferential tests[22m ([38;5;10mtranslation/tests/ffi_parity.rs[0m) load both [38;5;10m.so[0m files with [38;5;10mlibloading[0m and never call Rust directly, working bottom-up: [38;5;10mpack_u64le[0m → [38;5;10mmd5_addsample[0m → [38;5;10mupdate_md5[0m, plus a stateful test threading many calls through one live context. Roughly 30k cases: every single-bit [38;5;10mu64[0m, exhaustive [38;5;10mpos[0m 0–255 crossed with 14 [38;5;10mbits[0m values, [38;5;10mu32[0m/[38;5;10mu64[0m boundary values, sign-extension probes, and seeded fuzzing. Both the return value and the full 512-byte memory arena are compared byte-for-byte.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Two things worth calling out about the harness design:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mtflac_md5_addsample[0m's copy-back loop reads [38;5;10mbuffer[64 + bytes][0m for [38;5;10mbytes[0m up to 63, i.e. up to [38;5;10mbuffer[126][0m in a 72-byte buffer — past the end of the struct. That is what the C does, so both sides are handed a 512-byte arena with identical deterministic slack behind the struct, making those reads land on defined, equal bytes and keeping the comparison meaningful instead of accidentally comparing garbage.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10mupdate_md5[0m's [38;5;10msamples += 8 * sizeof(tflac_s32)[0m advances 32 elements while only 8 are read, so index 135 is the highest touched. Test inputs are sized accordingly and use distinct per-slot values so a wrong stride cannot alias into a passing result.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
I also confirmed the C struct layout with a compiled [38;5;10moffsetof[0m probe ([38;5;10mtflac_md5[0m = 88 bytes, [38;5;10mpos@0 total@8 buffer@16[0m; [38;5;10mtflac[0m = 96 bytes, [38;5;10mcur_blocksize@88 channels@92[0m), matching the [38;5;10mconst _[0m assertions in [38;5;10mlib.rs[0m and the offsets used by the tests.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mHarness validation:[22m because a passing differential suite is only as good as its sensitivity, I mutation-tested it — 12 injected defects (stride 32→8, loop 5→4 iterations, shifted byte lanes, [38;5;10mpos % 63[0m, copy-back source off-by-one, [38;5;10mtotal += bits/8[0m, double [38;5;10mb -= step[0m, dropped pack byte, [38;5;10mbytes/8 + 1[0m, [38;5;10mpos > 64[0m, post- vs pre-decrement, wrong sample index) were all detected. The only two mutants that survived are provably equivalent: [38;5;10m& 0xFF[0m makes sign- vs zero-extension unobservable, and an explicit padding field produces the identical layout. [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m was restored bit-identical afterward and re-verified.[0m[0m
